\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {47}{\ignorespaces The subsequent matched-reference comparison of two extraction geometries in the same 2015 functional-form study. Both exclude training bins out to $2.25\sigma _m$; one retains a $1.64\sigma _m$ extraction and a separate guard, while the other fits all bins inside $2.25\sigma _m$. The $z=0,1,3,5$ pull means and widths show similar conditional behavior. Together with the retained signal tails, this supported the widened blind/extraction window. Historical numerical values are unchanged.\relax }}{69}{figure.caption.56}\protected@file@percent }
