\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {54}{\ignorespaces Complete 19--250\nobreakspace  {}MeV observed search, with the preassigned active datasets shown above the curves. The upper panel shows 90\% CL$_\mathrm  {s}${} limits and the median, central 68\% and central 95\% ranges of the 300 conditional background-only toys per mass, with newly computed bands at the added 2015 coordinates. The next two panels show the fixed-mass asymptotic $p_0$ and its normal-quantile significance, with the local reference in black and the Sidak reference in red. The latter uses $N_{\rm  eff}=35.381$ for the complete search; its value at 66\nobreakspace  {}MeV is $Z_{\rm  Sidak}=1.305$, compared with local $Z=2.765$. The observed polyline connects every adjacent tested mass, including membership transitions; no numerical endpoint is changed by those connections. The physical visible-branching correction is applied once above the dimuon threshold. The expected bands are pointwise.\relax }}{84}{figure.caption.69}\protected@file@percent }
