\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {56}{\ignorespaces Current observed 90\% upper limits and the conditional full-2021 density-response proxy compared with the published BaBar visible-dark-photon observed 90\% contour \cite  {BaBarDarkPhoton2014}. The gray dashed curve is exactly the current maximal-available-dataset HPS result over 19--250\nobreakspace  {}MeV. The blue curve applies Eq.\nobreakspace  {}\textup  {\hbox {\mathsurround \z@ \normalfont  (\ignorespaces \ref  {eq:v501-density-proxy}\unskip \@@italiccorr )}} to its current observed normalization densities. It retains present fluctuations and is neither expected sensitivity nor a future observed limit or a fit to full-2021 data. HPS and BaBar use different statistical constructions. The coupling conversion includes the dimuon branching correction.\relax }}{87}{figure.caption.74}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:v501-babar-proxy}{{56}{87}{Current observed 90\% upper limits and the conditional full-2021 density-response proxy compared with the published BaBar visible-dark-photon observed 90\% contour \cite {BaBarDarkPhoton2014}. The gray dashed curve is exactly the current maximal-available-dataset HPS result over 19--250~MeV. The blue curve applies Eq.~\eqref {eq:v501-density-proxy} to its current observed normalization densities. It retains present fluctuations and is neither expected sensitivity nor a future observed limit or a fit to full-2021 data. HPS and BaBar use different statistical constructions. The coupling conversion includes the dimuon branching correction.\relax }{figure.caption.74}{}}
