\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {69}{\ignorespaces Common-coupling extraction at 66\nobreakspace  {}MeV, with a shared fitted amplitude $\setbox \z@ \hbox {\mathsurround \z@ $\textstyle \epsilon $}\mathaccent "0362{\epsilon }^2=4.55\times 10^{-6}$ and nominal local significance 2.76. Each campaign retains its own yield conversion and resolution. Bars show counting error only. Colored shading in the residuals is the zero-centered GP constraint width; it is neither fitted-background uncertainty nor total residual uncertainty.\relax }}{102}{figure.caption.89}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:v5-extraction-combined66}{{69}{102}{Common-coupling extraction at 66~MeV, with a shared fitted amplitude $\widehat \epsilon ^2=4.55\times 10^{-6}$ and nominal local significance 2.76. Each campaign retains its own yield conversion and resolution. Bars show counting error only. Colored shading in the residuals is the zero-centered GP constraint width; it is neither fitted-background uncertainty nor total residual uncertainty.\relax }{figure.caption.89}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {70}{\ignorespaces The 92\nobreakspace  {}MeV common-coupling fit now includes 2015, 2016 and 2021. It gives $\setbox \z@ \hbox {\mathsurround \z@ $\textstyle \epsilon $}\mathaccent "0362{\epsilon }^2=3.096\times 10^{-6}$ and nominal local $Z=2.520$. Top: observed counts, sideband GP mean and profiled signal-plus-background prediction. Bottom: observed counts minus that same unprofiled GP mean, with the fitted signal, the profiled-background shift, and their sum displayed separately. The last column sums common whole bins from the three campaigns and has no separate fit. Counting errors and the zero-centered GP constraint band omit post-fit covariance. The large standalone 2015 preferred rate is not the signal height imposed by this common fit; Section\nobreakspace  {}\ref  {sec:v5-rate-consistency} explains the comparison.\relax }}{103}{figure.caption.90}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:v5-extraction-combined92}{{70}{103}{The 92~MeV common-coupling fit now includes 2015, 2016 and 2021. It gives $\widehat \epsilon ^2=3.096\times 10^{-6}$ and nominal local $Z=2.520$. Top: observed counts, sideband GP mean and profiled signal-plus-background prediction. Bottom: observed counts minus that same unprofiled GP mean, with the fitted signal, the profiled-background shift, and their sum displayed separately. The last column sums common whole bins from the three campaigns and has no separate fit. Counting errors and the zero-centered GP constraint band omit post-fit covariance. The large standalone 2015 preferred rate is not the signal height imposed by this common fit; Section~\ref {sec:v5-rate-consistency} explains the comparison.\relax }{figure.caption.90}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {71}{\ignorespaces The deepest combined observed deficit at 72\nobreakspace  {}MeV has signed local significance $-3.49$ and an auxiliary amplitude $\setbox \z@ \hbox {\mathsurround \z@ $\textstyle \epsilon $}\mathaccent "0362{\epsilon }^2=-4.88\times 10^{-6}$. The negative signal template describes missing counts relative to the fitted background. Bars show counting error only; residual shading shows the zero-centered GP constraint width, not fitted-background or total residual uncertainty.\relax }}{104}{figure.caption.91}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:v5-extraction-combined72}{{71}{104}{The deepest combined observed deficit at 72~MeV has signed local significance $-3.49$ and an auxiliary amplitude $\widehat \epsilon ^2=-4.88\times 10^{-6}$. The negative signal template describes missing counts relative to the fitted background. Bars show counting error only; residual shading shows the zero-centered GP constraint width, not fitted-background or total residual uncertainty.\relax }{figure.caption.91}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {72}{\ignorespaces The earlier separated 2015 regions at 51 and 21\nobreakspace  {}MeV, with the added 92\nobreakspace  {}MeV region from the extension. The 21\nobreakspace  {}MeV feature is close to the lower search endpoint. All residuals subtract the unprofiled GP mean; the fitted signal, the background displacement and their sum are shown separately. Bars show counting errors and shading shows the GP constraint width, not a post-fit signal confidence band. The 92\nobreakspace  {}MeV panel is an individual 2015 fit; its preferred amplitude differs from the common-rate extraction in Figure\nobreakspace  {}\ref  {fig:v5-extraction-combined92}.\relax }}{105}{figure.caption.92}\protected@file@percent }
