\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {80}{\ignorespaces Profiled 2015 conditional local and global probabilities on 19--100\nobreakspace  {}MeV. The full field uses 82 integer hypotheses and the endpoint kernel prescription in Appendix\nobreakspace  {}\ref  {app:v504-extension}. Its response matrix and the first 256 coherent Poisson scans are reused from the extended covariance study; 200,000 Gaussian fields integrate the enlarged search. Open symbols retain one-sided 95\% bounds for empty direct tails. Probability and $Z^+$ panels refer to the declared stress model. The interpretation, sigcorr check and sampling method are in Appendix\nobreakspace  {}\ref  {app:v504-global-study}.\relax }}{116}{figure.caption.103}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:v5-global-2015}{{80}{116}{Profiled 2015 conditional local and global probabilities on 19--100~MeV. The full field uses 82 integer hypotheses and the endpoint kernel prescription in Appendix~\ref {app:v504-extension}. Its response matrix and the first 256 coherent Poisson scans are reused from the extended covariance study; 200,000 Gaussian fields integrate the enlarged search. Open symbols retain one-sided 95\% bounds for empty direct tails. Probability and $Z^+$ panels refer to the declared stress model. The interpretation, sigcorr check and sampling method are in Appendix~\ref {app:v504-global-study}.\relax }{figure.caption.103}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {81}{\ignorespaces Profiled 2016 conditional global study with the same black-local/red-global convention and integer $Z^+$ guides. Ordinary sampling uses 2,000,000 fields; targeted importance sampling resolves the previously empty Gaussian tails without altering the field model or ordering. At 42\nobreakspace  {}MeV the conditional Gaussian global probability is $6.096\times 10^{-20}$ ($Z=9.067$), with 0.16\% relative Monte Carlo standard error. This extreme value reflects the biased stress reference, not a particle discovery. The direct Poisson check remains 0/1,000, giving only $p<0.002991$ ($Z>2.749$); its open triangles retain those bounds. Red shading gives sampling intervals, not background-model uncertainty. This global calculation is different from the Sidak reference. The implementation and stress-reference diagnostics are in Appendix\nobreakspace  {}\ref  {app:v504-global-study}.\relax }}{117}{figure.caption.104}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:v5-global-2016}{{81}{117}{Profiled 2016 conditional global study with the same black-local/red-global convention and integer $Z^+$ guides. Ordinary sampling uses 2,000,000 fields; targeted importance sampling resolves the previously empty Gaussian tails without altering the field model or ordering. At 42~MeV the conditional Gaussian global probability is $6.096\times 10^{-20}$ ($Z=9.067$), with 0.16\% relative Monte Carlo standard error. This extreme value reflects the biased stress reference, not a particle discovery. The direct Poisson check remains 0/1,000, giving only $p<0.002991$ ($Z>2.749$); its open triangles retain those bounds. Red shading gives sampling intervals, not background-model uncertainty. This global calculation is different from the Sidak reference. The implementation and stress-reference diagnostics are in Appendix~\ref {app:v504-global-study}.\relax }{figure.caption.104}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {82}{\ignorespaces Profiled study for the released 2021 10\% sample. The principal ordering selects 92\nobreakspace  {}MeV and gives GP global probability 0.02519 ($Z=1.957$), with 26/1,000 direct exceedances. The GP ensemble retains 200,000 fields. Black is the conditional local probability and red the global probability, with the corresponding $Z^+$ below. This global calculation uses the correlated field rather than the Sidak correction used for the asymptotic references. Qualification of the generating background remains required for a particle-global interpretation. The implementation and stress-reference diagnostics are in Appendix\nobreakspace  {}\ref  {app:v504-global-study}.\relax }}{118}{figure.caption.105}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:v5-global-2021}{{82}{118}{Profiled study for the released 2021 10\% sample. The principal ordering selects 92~MeV and gives GP global probability 0.02519 ($Z=1.957$), with 26/1,000 direct exceedances. The GP ensemble retains 200,000 fields. Black is the conditional local probability and red the global probability, with the corresponding $Z^+$ below. This global calculation uses the correlated field rather than the Sidak correction used for the asymptotic references. Qualification of the generating background remains required for a particle-global interpretation. The implementation and stress-reference diagnostics are in Appendix~\ref {app:v504-global-study}.\relax }{figure.caption.105}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {83}{\ignorespaces Combined conditional field over the complete 19--250\nobreakspace  {}MeV search, with all three campaigns active through 100\nobreakspace  {}MeV. The ten changed coordinates use new joint-likelihood responses to the same 1,626 histogram-bin directions; all 256 direct experiments remain coherent over the entire grid. Gaussian tails use 200,000 ordinary fields and 40,000 conditional-mixture draws at every positive-fit threshold with standardized score at least 3.5. At 76\nobreakspace  {}MeV the conditional global probability is $1.351\times 10^{-17}$, but the raw fit is only $r=0.166$: this is a stress-reference mismatch. Empty direct tails give only $p<0.01163$. Appendix\nobreakspace  {}\ref  {app:v504-global-study} explains the estimator, and Appendix\nobreakspace  {}\ref  {app:v504-width-review} explains the narrow display feature. Historical values for the former membership are retained in Appendix\nobreakspace  {}\ref  {app:v504-historical-displays}.\relax }}{119}{figure.caption.106}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:v5-global-combined}{{83}{119}{Combined conditional field over the complete 19--250~MeV search, with all three campaigns active through 100~MeV. The ten changed coordinates use new joint-likelihood responses to the same 1,626 histogram-bin directions; all 256 direct experiments remain coherent over the entire grid. Gaussian tails use 200,000 ordinary fields and 40,000 conditional-mixture draws at every positive-fit threshold with standardized score at least 3.5. At 76~MeV the conditional global probability is $1.351\times 10^{-17}$, but the raw fit is only $r=0.166$: this is a stress-reference mismatch. Empty direct tails give only $p<0.01163$. Appendix~\ref {app:v504-global-study} explains the estimator, and Appendix~\ref {app:v504-width-review} explains the narrow display feature. Historical values for the former membership are retained in Appendix~\ref {app:v504-historical-displays}.\relax }{figure.caption.106}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {84}{\ignorespaces Discovery probabilities and aligned $Z^+$ values for all four overlapping combinations. Local asymptotic curves are black and Sidak global references are red. Each pair of panels shares its mass axis and uses one fixed $N_{\rm  eff}$ over that scope's full overlap, now through 100\nobreakspace  {}MeV whenever 2015 participates. The 90--100\nobreakspace  {}MeV extension is shaded. These are analytic Sidak references, distinct from the stress-centered correlated-field global probabilities above; no additional correction for selecting among overlapping scopes is included.\relax }}{120}{figure.caption.107}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:v502-combination-discovery}{{84}{120}{Discovery probabilities and aligned $Z^+$ values for all four overlapping combinations. Local asymptotic curves are black and Sidak global references are red. Each pair of panels shares its mass axis and uses one fixed $N_{\rm eff}$ over that scope's full overlap, now through 100~MeV whenever 2015 participates. The 90--100~MeV extension is shaded. These are analytic Sidak references, distinct from the stress-centered correlated-field global probabilities above; no additional correction for selecting among overlapping scopes is included.\relax }{figure.caption.107}{}}
