\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {86}{\ignorespaces Separate campaign coupling estimates with local curvature errors and the common fitted rate at 66, 92, 72 and 76\nobreakspace  {}MeV. All three campaigns now enter every comparison. At 92\nobreakspace  {}MeV the common fit gives $\setbox \z@ \hbox {\mathsurround \z@ $\textstyle \epsilon $}\mathaccent "0362{\epsilon }^2=3.096\times 10^{-6}$; freeing the three rates lowers twice the negative log likelihood by 11.552, compared with 2.845 at 66\nobreakspace  {}MeV. The shaded band is the common fit's local curvature interval. These selected comparisons are descriptive; the errors are not post-selection intervals and no unadjusted compatibility probability is assigned.\relax }}{124}{figure.caption.110}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:v5-consistency}{{86}{124}{Separate campaign coupling estimates with local curvature errors and the common fitted rate at 66, 92, 72 and 76~MeV. All three campaigns now enter every comparison. At 92~MeV the common fit gives $\widehat \epsilon ^2=3.096\times 10^{-6}$; freeing the three rates lowers twice the negative log likelihood by 11.552, compared with 2.845 at 66~MeV. The shaded band is the common fit's local curvature interval. These selected comparisons are descriptive; the errors are not post-selection intervals and no unadjusted compatibility probability is assigned.\relax }{figure.caption.110}{}}
