\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {90}{\ignorespaces Representative background-only distributions from the saved 1,000 complete Poisson scans. Green histograms show the signed fitted coordinate, gold curves the unfluctuated-response Gaussian approximation, and black lines the observed fit. These panels show why the apparently large centered scores at 2016 42\nobreakspace  {}MeV and combined 76\nobreakspace  {}MeV can coexist with nearly zero raw observed fits. At 2016 76\nobreakspace  {}MeV the observed fit is negative and is excluded by the positive-fit gate. Agreement of the histograms with the gold curves tests the approximation under that reference, not the physical correctness of the reference spectrum.\relax }}{143}{figure.caption.120}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:v502-stress-distributions}{{90}{143}{Representative background-only distributions from the saved 1,000 complete Poisson scans. Green histograms show the signed fitted coordinate, gold curves the unfluctuated-response Gaussian approximation, and black lines the observed fit. These panels show why the apparently large centered scores at 2016 42~MeV and combined 76~MeV can coexist with nearly zero raw observed fits. At 2016 76~MeV the observed fit is negative and is excluded by the positive-fit gate. Agreement of the histograms with the gold curves tests the approximation under that reference, not the physical correctness of the reference spectrum.\relax }{figure.caption.120}{}}
